# SPEC: §4, §16
# ERROR_KIND: name
# ERROR: Sprint 34
# EXIT: 1
#
# THE DEFERRAL, TESTED RATHER THAN PROMISED.
#
# Invariant 3 says an unimplemented path hard-errors NAMING ITS
# SPRINT.  That is a claim about behaviour, so it gets a test: `bind`
# must raise "name" and the message must say Sprint 34, not report a
# typo.  A user who writes `bind("<C-p>", ...)` today has to be told
# the feature is coming, because "undefined name 'bind'" sends them
# looking for a spelling mistake that is not there.
#
# WHEN SPRINT 34 LANDS, this file is rewritten into real coverage and
# the ledger picks it up unchanged -- the `# SPEC:` line is what keys
# it, not the name.
bind("H", "s", fn() { return 1 })
